<title>UK: Flood relief flights leave UK for Poland, Romania.</title>
<headline>Flood relief flights leave UK for Poland, Romania.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK-based air cargo management company AirRep said it has flown two flood relief cargo charter flights from Manston airport in the UK to Bucharest and Warsaw over the past 10 days.</p>
<p>The flights were contracted by UK-based Air Foyle and operated on behalf of the Japan government's Japan International Co-operation Agency (JICA).</p>
<p>They were flown by AirRep management client, Bulgarian airline Inter Trans Air with fully-loaded 20-tonne capacity Antonov AN-12 aircraft.</p>
<p>Martin said the flights carried relief equipment including blankets and medicines for flood victims.</p>
<p>&quot;JICA is a new customer to us,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
